## Impact
A weakness has been found that lets someone get around the rule that a proposal needs a certain amount of support to be approved in the ExtraordinaryFunding contract. By using this weakness, a bad person could make proposals go through even if they didn't have enough support. This could lead to them taking tokens from the treasury without permission, which would cause the organization to lose money and let them control the funding system.

## Proof of Concept
The problem is with the "extraordinaryProposalSucceeded" function. It is called when the "executeExtraordinary" function runs. This function checks if a proposal can be executed successfully. To determine this, it calculates a minimum threshold based on the percentage of tokens requested in the proposal compared to the total tokens in the treasury. However, there is a mistake in the calculation because it uses the wrong value for the total tokens in the treasury.

Specifically, the _getSliceOfTreasury function used to calculate the total tokens available in the treasury uses the value of 1e18 minus the minimum threshold percentage, instead of 1e18. This means that the minimum threshold required for a proposal to succeed is calculated incorrectly and can be easily bypassed.

